    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0121" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3444: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Nanking (Peck)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-08T17:00:00-05:00">January 8, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Your 4, January 8, 2 p.m., and 5, January 8, 5 p.m. This Government’s note of
                    January 7 envisages provisions of all treaties by virtue of which the United
                    States has rights in and with regard to <pb facs="0122" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/>
                    Manchuria. Without making any commitment, either affirmative or negative, with
                    regard to its future course of action, which course will depend on developments,
                    the Department perceives at present no immediate occasion for calling a
                    conference and believes that it would not be opportune under existing
                    circumstances to propose that step.</p>
                <p>You may so inform Foreign Minister orally and Department will so inform Chinese
                    Minister here.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Peiping as Dept’s No. 8.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
